From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:50:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] shaders/colorspace: the reshaping picks its piece by the
 sample as it is, not by the sample clamped to the pivots

pl_shader_dovi_reshape() clamps each component to the range of its pivots
and then chooses the piece of the curve by comparing that clamped value
with the pivots. Clause 5.4.2.2 of ETSI GS CCM 001 chooses the piece with
the sample as it is (pivot_idx is the first piece whose upper pivot the
sample is below, the last piece for a sample at or above the last pivot),
and clauses 5.4.2.3.2 and 5.4.2.3.3 then clamp the sample to the pivots for
the mapping itself.

The two agree unless the first two pivots are the same code, which the
clause allows (Assign_pivot_values() makes each pivot the one before it
plus pred_pivot_value, and that can be 0; libplacebo-9930 composes such a
curve as the clause says). A sample below that first pivot is clamped up to
it, and the clamped value is not below the second pivot, which is the same
code: the reshaping took the piece after the empty one, where the clause
takes the first piece. The mapping then used the wrong piece's
coefficients for every sample below the first pivot.

The piece is now chosen with the component's value as it is. Everything
else is as before: the clamp to the pivots for the mapping, the clamp of
the other components for the MMR mapping, the result clamped to [0, 1].
For pivots that increase strictly the two choices are the same for every
sample, so the output does not change.

Checked on Mesa's zink with a component of three pieces (pivots 0.25,
0.25, 0.5, 1) against the clause on 1025 samples of 0 to 1: the old
shader gives the second piece below 0.25, the new one the first, as the
clause does; with strictly increasing pivots both agree with the clause on
all of them.
---
 src/shaders/colorspace.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/shaders/colorspace.c b/src/shaders/colorspace.c
index 67ff998..459bfcf 100644
--- a/src/shaders/colorspace.c
+++ b/src/shaders/colorspace.c
@@ -182,6 +182,7 @@ void pl_shader_dovi_reshape(pl_shader sh, const struct pl_dovi_metadata *data)
          "vec3 sig;                             \n"
          "vec4 coeffs;                          \n"
          "float s;                              \n"
+         "float sel;                            \n"
          "sig = clamp(color.rgb, "$", "$");     \n",
          sh_var(sh, (struct pl_shader_var) {
              .var  = pl_var_vec3("pivot_lo"),
@@ -201,7 +202,10 @@ void pl_shader_dovi_reshape(pl_shader sh, const struct pl_dovi_metadata *data)
             continue;
 
         pl_assert(comp->num_pivots >= 2 && comp->num_pivots <= 9);
-        GLSL("s = sig[%d]; \n", c);
+        // The sample is clamped to the pivots for the mapping, but the piece it
+        // maps with is the one of the sample as it is (ETSI GS CCM 001 5.4.2.2)
+        GLSL("s = sig[%d]; \n"
+             "sel = color[%d]; \n", c, c);
 
         // Prepare coefficients for GPU
         bool has_poly = false, has_mmr = false, mmr_single = true;
@@ -278,7 +282,7 @@ void pl_shader_dovi_reshape(pl_shader sh, const struct pl_dovi_metadata *data)
             });
 
             // Efficiently branch into the correct set of coefficients
-            GLSL("#define test(i) bvec4(s >= "$"[i])                \n"
+            GLSL("#define test(i) bvec4(sel >= "$"[i])              \n"
                  "#define coef(i) "$"[i]                            \n"
                  "coeffs = mix(mix(mix(coef(0), coef(1), test(0)),  \n"
                  "                 mix(coef(2), coef(3), test(2)),  \n"
